data emit_on_demand_family_cadence_note: String = "The seven emit-on-demand family aggregates (9 witness families: add, field_access, complement, match, loop, fold_closure, meet_join, variant_construct, classical_not_ingested) enroll on this nightly Wet cadence 2026-07-21: each emits real Rust, cargo-builds under the permitted build_workspace_grant envelope, runs the native binary, and compares against the interpreted oracle. Enrolled after the 2026-07-20 regression proved the class was invisible to CI (test/claim/execution/ excluded from hermetic discovery AND offline roster - the enrolled-but-never-run coverage-by-illusion class): the sorted_fields interner-order bug broke all 9 families' wet legs and nothing red-ed. This cadence is the rot-detector. Per-PR stays hermetic; the full CI-on-v2 cutover (P6) additionally needs the content-keyed result store so builds amortize. The former carrier-specific intrinsic seam is dissolved onto std.access Permit/Deny."

data falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_note: String = "Wet expect_red quarantine for SelfEmitted module behavioral receipts that red on assemble (Phase-0 admission invariant, review #7199 2026-07-25): same mechanism as known_red_probe_entries but Wet-profiled — hermetic would refuse the host effect and lie about the red class. claim_executor expect_red-inverts the batch. Owner: #7199 falsifier lane / self-host assemble. Dissolve-on per row: local wet receipt greens under gunbc_falsifier_self_host_wet_receipt_wall_budget, the known-red entry deletes, and the SelfHostWetReceiptBinding restores to seed_emitter_behavioral_wet_module_bindings."

data falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries: List<std.realization_schedule.ScheduleWitnessEntry> = v2.compiler.self_host.seed_emitter_behavioral_wet_known_red_entries.seed_emitter_behavioral_wet_known_red_entries

fn falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_batch_enrolled() -> Bool {
  length(xs: falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries) > 0
}

fn falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_roster() -> List<std.realization_schedule.ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries
}

fn schedule_entry_from_binding(b: v2.compiler.self_host.seed_emitter_behavioral_wet_module_bindings.SelfHostWetReceiptBinding) -> std.realization_schedule.ScheduleWitnessEntry {
  self_host_wet_entry(entry: b.entry, f: b.function)
}

data wet_enrollment_roster_term_deleted_note: String = "The frontier-enrolled term is gone with the self-host frontier roster, and it was already empty. falsifier_self_host_wet_entries formerly appended a fold over the roster that admitted a row only when find_wet_receipt_binding matched its module_path; no row matched, which is precisely what falsifier_self_host_wet_template_only_holds asserted by requiring that term to have length zero. So the wet falsifier lane ran on template entries alone before the deletion and runs on template entries alone after it, with no entry added, removed or reordered.

That gate is retired rather than weakened: it claimed the roster enrolls nothing, and there is no roster left to enroll anything. What survives is the binding lookup itself (find_wet_receipt_binding, schedule_entry_from_binding), which is keyed on a module path and needs no roster to be asked."

fn falsifier_self_host_wet_entries() -> List<std.realization_schedule.ScheduleWitnessEntry> {
  falsifier_self_host_wet_template_entries
}
